# Component Prop Namespacing

Injected child props go under one lowercase key named for the component:

```jsx
cloneElement(child, { fold: { isOpen, toggle } })
// not: cloneElement(child, { isOpen, toggle })

const FoldTrigger = ({ fold: { isOpen, toggle } = {}, children }) => ...
```

## Exception: data templates

Components that iterate a data collection into a template child (`Grid`,
`VirtualGrid`, `Masonry`, `Map`) inject the datum as top-level `item` and
`index` props instead. This is one shared contract, so the same card template
works under any of them:

```jsx
cloneElement(child, { item, index })

const Card = ({ item, index }) => ...
```

This applies only to the iterated datum. Controller/context injection
(`fold`, `mediaLightbox`, `multiSelect`, `tabs`, `viewSwitch`, `minimap`)
stays namespaced, including on these same components.
